inside FBI headquarters the Acting  Director is pushing agents to focus on  their work Andrew McCabe has taken over  the Russian investigation as commis  replacement president Trump met with  McCabe for a second time yesterday to  discuss the bureau there are reports  that morale has taken a hit after commis  firing Jeff pjs is outside FBI  headquarters in Washington Jeff good  morning good morning the White House  isn't wasting any time it is moving  quickly to find an interim FBI director  until the president chooses commis  permanent replacement the firings  stunned the FBI which is right in the  midst of this Russia investigation one  of the most important in its history  it's one of at least five people who  have already been interviewed at the  Justice Department for the job of  interim director of the FBI according to  sources the way Comey found out about  his dismissal surprised some inside the  bureau he was visiting the Los Angeles  field office talking with agents when  news reports flashed on TV screens that  he had been fired many field agents also  received the news through the media he  was no longer had the confidence of the  President or the rest of the FBI some  Bureau agents and employees tell CBS  News they took issue with White House  spokesperson Sarah Huckabee Sanders  claimed that Comey lost the confidence  of rank-and-file FBI employees Timothy  Murphy is a former Deputy Director of  the FBI director Comey was well liked by  the employees you may have had a number  of employees in the organization that  may have disagreed with his approach on  his handling of the email investigation  but overall director Comey built up a  lot of goodwill in the FBI about the way  he treated people the respect he had for  the employees of the organization law  enforcement sources tell CBS News that  the FBI Russia investigation had been  picking up speed in recent weeks FBI  agents in the US and overseas have been  intensely focusing on following the  money 